WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:08.164
Ally was still fast asleep when the music started playing.

2
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:13.771
"Not today, Alpha," she said with a groan.

3
00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:17.394
But as Ally pulled up the blankets, sadness washed over her.

4
00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:23.618
She wasn't in the pod—she was in the sewing room at Mateo's house.

5
00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:30.454
She blinked open her eyes. "Where's that music coming from?"

6
00:00:30.455 --> 00:00:34.030
"From out here!" Mateo called through the closed door.

7
00:00:34.031 --> 00:00:37.535
"Isn't this how Alpha wakes you up every day?"

8
00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:47.574
Ally didn't want to make Mateo feel bad, so she tried to wipe away her sadness. "Come on in."

9
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:52.698
"You have to work," Mateo said, "but I have the whole day to look for the pod.

10
00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:57.396
I'll go to the museum as soon as it opens. But first check this out."

11
00:00:57.397 --> 00:01:02.306
He read from an article on his phone: 'New City-Wide Parking Ordinance.

12
00:01:02.307 --> 00:01:07.419
The city of Sandville has begun implementing its new zero-tolerance policy.

13
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.146
All illegally parked vehicles will be towed to the impound lot.'

14
00:01:12.147 --> 00:01:15.666
"Maybe your pod got towed," Mateo said excitedly.

15
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:19.149
"Let's go to the impound lot before your shift begins."

16
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:27.842
"I'll be ready in a flash!" Ally cried.

17
00:01:27.843 --> 00:01:33.333
*** At the impound lot, there was a long line of humans waiting to claim their cars.

18
00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:38.197
"This will take all day!" Ally moaned.

19
00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:49.370
"Maybe not." Mateo pointed to an area marked Oversize and Special Use Vehicles.

20
00:01:49.371 --> 00:01:56.286
They walked past parked campers, school buses, and a house on wheels.

21
00:01:56.287 --> 00:01:59.096
But Ally's pod wasn't there.

22
00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:02.872
"I really thought we would find it here," Mateo said.

23
00:02:02.873 --> 00:02:07.088
"I'll go to the museum now and meet you at the diner later."

24
00:02:07.089 --> 00:02:11.991
"Thanks, Mateo," Ally said as they headed in different directions.

25
00:02:11.992 --> 00:02:15.143
"Think positive," she told herself.

26
00:02:15.144 --> 00:02:18.106
"Hello there!" someone called.

27
00:02:18.107 --> 00:02:22.057
Ally looked up. It was the artist, Sarah.

28
00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:24.928
"Thanks for the suggestion about the park.

29
00:02:24.929 --> 00:02:31.017
I found some amazing objects there—and a perfect location for my new sculpture!"

30
00:02:31.018 --> 00:02:34.955
Ally smiled. "I'm glad I was helpful."

31
00:02:34.956 --> 00:02:40.848
"I'd love to show you the site," Sarah said. "Are you free now?"

32
00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:52.096
"I have to go to work," Ally said, "but I'll stop by later."

33
00:02:52.097 --> 00:02:58.720
*** When Ally arrived at the diner, Barry was pacing

34
00:02:58.721 --> 00:03:01.539
around. "I thought you'd never get here!" he

35
00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.698
said. "I really want to learn how to levitate plates before the League of Rocket Scientists

36
00:03:06.699 --> 00:03:13.295
gala." Ally took a deep breath and reminded herself to be

37
00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:20.010
patient. "That's not realistic, Barry," she said. "It takes a long time to learn a trick like

38
00:03:20.011 --> 00:03:24.976
that." Barry frowned. "Well, I'm a super-fast

39
00:03:24.977 --> 00:03:28.691
learner." "Okay." Ally

40
00:03:28.692 --> 00:03:35.952
shrugged. "Let's get started. The first step is learning to make it look like you're stumbling without

41
00:03:35.953 --> 00:03:45.456
falling." "I've been practicing that skill. Watch this!" Barry demonstrated a perfect fake

42
00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:47.448
stumble. "Whoa," Ally

43
00:03:47.449 --> 00:03:55.525
thought. "He has been practicing! I guess it's time for the next part of my plan. I hope it

44
00:03:55.526 --> 00:04:00.376
works." Ally reached under the counter and pulled out the bag of mattress springs that she and Mateo had

45
00:04:00.377 --> 00:04:07.905
gotten. Next she found a package of magnets they'd used while redecorating the

46
00:04:07.906 --> 00:04:12.698
diner. "I'm going to glue a magnet on one end of this spring," Ally

47
00:04:12.699 --> 00:04:18.142
said. "Then you'll slip your finger through the spring on the other

48
00:04:18.143 --> 00:04:24.029
end." "So the magnet will stick to the plate?" Barry asked.

49
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.461
"How?" "Um . . ." Ally had forgotten that

50
00:04:28.462 --> 00:04:35.870
detail. "We put another magnet on the bottom of the plate, of course!

51
00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:42.043
Why don't you take care of the customers, and I'll get this trick set up."

52
00:04:42.044 --> 00:04:47.871
After Ally had gotten everything together, she called Barry back over.

53
00:04:47.872 --> 00:04:57.435
"Practice with a paper plate. That way you can get the feel of the trick, without breaking anything."

54
00:04:57.436 --> 00:05:02.862
Barry slipped the spring through his finger and then took a practice stumble.

55
00:05:02.863 --> 00:05:09.559
Ally was relieved when the plate stayed on the spring.

56
00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.509
He spun toward her, his eyes narrowed.

57
00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:20.337
"Why don't I ever see the spring when you do it? And how do you stick magnets to customers' plates?"

58
00:05:20.338 --> 00:05:22.846
Ally crossed her fingers behind her back.

59
00:05:22.847 --> 00:05:27.455
"I've been practicing a long time. You'll have to practice a lot.

60
00:05:27.456 --> 00:05:30.694
And remember, use paper plates for now!"

61
00:05:30.695 --> 00:05:35.597
She hurried off to take care of customers.

62
00:05:35.598 --> 00:05:40.586
A minute later she saw Barry stumble, a bowl of cold cereal attached to the spring.

63
00:05:40.587 --> 00:05:43.034
At first it looked like the trick was going to work.

64
00:05:43.035 --> 00:05:48.399
But then he lost his footing and tripped for real.

65
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.322
The bowl flew through the air—and splash!

66
00:05:51.323 --> 00:05:56.931
It landed in a customer's lap!

